    "Navigation uses a custom route-based system (AppRouterState + ScreenRouteRegistry/AppRouteCatalog) instead of Jetpack Navigation Component. The 'navController' passed to screens is from rememberNavController() but is not used for composable-based navigation.",
    "Screen sealed class with data objects/screen registrations is the core navigation abstraction. Route IDs follow 'native.<snake_case_name>' pattern, automatically derived from Screen subclass simple names.",
    "Tool packages (ToolPkg) can dynamically register additional routes (TOOLPKG_COMPOSE_DSL runtime) and navigation entries via PackageManager.",
    "Phone (<600dp) uses PhoneLayout with modal Drawer navigation; Tablet (>=600dp) uses TabletLayout with a sidebar that can expand/collapse.",
    "Navigation drawer content is in ui/main/components/DrawerContent.kt and ui/main/components/NavigationComponents.kt.",
    "All Activities are ComponentActivity or Activity subclasses. No Fragment-based UI is used - the app is 100% Jetpack Compose.",
    "No QuickSettings TileService found.",
    "Two App Widgets using Glance (Modern Android Widget framework): VoiceAssistantWidgetReceiver and ToolPkgDesktopWidgetReceiver.",
    "Floating windows are implemented via SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW permission (WindowManager overlay), managed by FloatingChatService and UIDebuggerService.",
    "Voice interaction uses Android's VoiceInteractionService framework for system default assistant integration.",
    "The OperitApp composable hosts all screens and uses a custom RouterState stack for back navigation.",
    "Settings has 23 sub-screens accessible from the main SettingsScreen, all located in ui/features/settings/screens/ directory.",
